================================================================================
UPSTREAM CREDITS / 上游工作致谢
================================================================================

LensKD builds upon and extends the following prior work. These are independent
research contributions by their respective authors and are credited here for
transparency. See the "与论文的关系" (Relationship to Prior Work) section of
README.md for a precise statement of what LensKD adds to each.

  - Dual-Space Knowledge Distillation (DSKD)
    Zhang et al., EMNLP 2024.  https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.17328
    LensKD's contribution: identifies and quantifies the projector-induced
    distribution flattening (entropy 1.33 -> 7.33), and introduces a
    dual-path fusion that restores the sharp native signal.

  - A Dual-Space Framework for General Knowledge Distillation of LLMs
    Zhang et al., 2025 (extended version).  https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.11426
    Source of the projector formulation and the Exact Token Alignment (ETA)
    algorithm that LensKD adopts and re-implements.

  - On-Policy Distillation of Language Models (GKD)
    Agarwal et al., ICLR 2024.  https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.13649
    LensKD's contribution: progressive lambda schedule and down-sampled
    self-sampling, plus the finding that pure on-policy (lambda=1) is unusable
    at a 23x capacity gap.

  - MiniLLM: On-Policy Distillation of Large Language Models
    Gu et al., ICLR 2024.  https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.08543
    Source of the reverse-KL (mode-seeking) objective.

  - ToDi: Token-wise Distillation via Fine-Grained Divergence Control
    Jung et al., EMNLP 2025.  https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.16297
    Source of per-token forward/reverse KL mixing.

  - Entropy-Aware On-Policy Distillation of Language Models (EOPD)
    Jin et al., ICML 2026.  https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.07079
    Source of entropy-driven gating as a difficulty signal.

  - TinyBERT: Distilling BERT for Natural Language Understanding
    Jiao et al., Findings of EMNLP 2020.  https://arxiv.org/abs/1909.10351
    Source of intermediate-layer representation alignment.

